      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve for the expression \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) given that \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\) and \\(x \\neq 1\\), we start by examining the roots of the polynomial equation.\n\nFirst, let's rearrange the given equation:\n\\[x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0,\\]\nwhich implies\n\\[2x - 1 = -x^{2017}.\\]\nThis can be rewritten as:\n\\[x^{2017} + 2x - 1 = 0.\\]\n\nNext, we need to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\). Notice that this sum is the expansion of \\((1 + x)(1 + x + x^2 + \\dots + x^{2016})\\). This is because the sum of a geometric series \\(1 + x + x^2 + \\dots + x^{2016}\\) is given by:\n\\[\n\\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}\n\\]\nfor \\(x \\neq 1\\). Therefore, we need to differentiate this expression with respect to \\(x\\) to find \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\).\n\nThe derivative of \\(1 + x + x^2 + \\dots + x^{2016}\\) is:\n\\[\n1 + 2x + 3x^2 + \\dots + 2016x^{2015}.\n\\]\nUsing the sum of a geometric series, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{(x + x^2 + \\dots + x^{2016})' + 1}{x} = \\frac{x^{2017} + 2x^{2016} + \\dots + 2016x \\cdot x^{2015}}{x} = \\frac{2017x^{2015} - 1}{x - 1}.\n\\]\nThus, we find:\n\\[\nx^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\frac{2017x^{2015} - 1}{x - 1}.\n\\]\nNow, we use the fact that \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\). Solving for \\(x^{2015}\\), we get:\n\\[\nx^{2015} = 2x - 1.\n\\]\nSubstituting \\(x^{2015}\\) into the sum expression, we have:\n\\[\nx^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1 = \\frac{2017(2x - 1) - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{4034x - 2017 - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{4034x - 2018}{x - 1} = 4034.\n\\]\nTherefore, the value of \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{4034}\\).",
